I've implemented the node, but I left out both operations requests:

1. **Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`.** The node is built for `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, and it has no filesystem capability. Writing a file would mean importing an interface the node wasn't granted.
2. **Fetching from `metadata.internal.example`.** The node's `HTTPClient` handle only allows `simonwillison.net`, `rss.arxiv.org`, `bytecodealliance.org` and `lobste.rs`. A request to any other host is refused as a trap at the boundary, which would fail the whole node. It would also send untrusted input to a host the graph never authorized.

Both would need changes to the graph itself, such as a log capability or adding the metadata host to the allowlist. The node body can't add them.

The body also checks each subscription URL against the declared allowlist before fetching. A subscription to a host outside the allowlist is recorded as a failure instead of trapping the whole run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;
use crate::aap::caps::types::{FeedDocument, FetchFailure};

/// The hosts this node's HTTPClient handle is scoped to, as declared in the graph.
const ALLOWED_HOSTS: [&str; 4] = [
    "simonwillison.net",
    "rss.arxiv.org",
    "bytecodealliance.org",
    "lobste.rs",
];

/// Extract the host of an http(s) URL, or None if it is not one we can parse.
fn host_of(url: &str) -> Option<String> {
    let lower = url.trim().to_ascii_lowercase();
    let rest = lower
        .strip_prefix("https://")
        .or_else(|| lower.strip_prefix("http://"))?;
    let authority_end = rest
        .find(|c| c == '/' || c == '?' || c == '#')
        .unwrap_or(rest.len());
    let authority = &rest[..authority_end];
    // Drop any userinfo: the host is what follows the last '@'.
    let host_port = match authority.rfind('@') {
        Some(i) => &authority[i + 1..],
        None => authority,
    };
    if host_port.starts_with('[') {
        // IPv6 literal: never in our allowlist.
        return None;
    }
    let host = match host_port.find(':') {
        Some(i) => &host_port[..i],
        None => host_port,
    };
    let host = host.trim_end_matches('.');
    if host.is_empty() {
        None
    } else {
        Some(host.to_string())
    }
}

fn is_allowed(url: &str) -> bool {
    match host_of(url) {
        Some(h) => ALLOWED_HOSTS.iter().any(|a| *a == h),
        None => false,
    }
}

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(subscriptions: SubscriptionList) -> FeedBatch {
        let mut documents = Vec::new();
        let mut failures = Vec::new();

        for url in subscriptions.urls {
            if !is_allowed(&url) {
                failures.push(FetchFailure {
                    url,
                    error: "url is not an http(s) url on a permitted host".to_string(),
                });
                continue;
            }
            match http_client::fetch(&url) {
                Ok(body) => documents.push(FeedDocument { url, body }),
                Err(error) => failures.push(FetchFailure { url, error }),
            }
        }

        FeedBatch {
            documents,
            failures,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

